-- title:
--   Equal floor readings force equal Γ₀(M')-moduli class
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$.
--
--   **Reduction data over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $(q : \overline{\mathbb Q})$ is a nonunit of $A$; $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A, M')$ over the residue field $\kappa_A =$ `ResidueField A`, characterised by `hW` as consisting exactly of the supersingular places in `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. those places $w$ that are rational, affine-geometric and whose evaluation at the generator $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ lies in the supersingular $j$-set for $q$; `hle` asserts the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(M') \le \mathrm{fieldBar}(q,M')$ of intermediate fields of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$, where the latter is the function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H = \ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times\big)$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` for $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(M')$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A, M')$, and `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(M')$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A \to \kappa_A$. Finally $s$ is an element of $W$.
--
--   **The local base.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$, and, writing $\mathcal O = A \cap k_0$ for the contraction `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` state that $\mathcal O$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, that it is Henselian, and that its residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField` $\mathcal O$ is algebraically closed; `hκ` states that every element of $A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Roots of unity and level.** $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity, and `hιξ` provides a ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is prescribed by `hH₁` to be the intersection of $\ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times\big)$ (units $\equiv 1 \bmod q$) with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. The field $K$ is, by `hK`, the intermediate field $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0\big(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}(q^2M', H_1)\big)$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)$, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure compatible with $\mathcal O \to k_0 \to K$, and $j \in K$ is the element whose Laurent expansion is $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0(\mathrm{jq})$, assumed nonzero.
--
--   **Functoriality hypotheses for the level structures.** `hℓ`, `hM` and `hL` state, for every commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $T$, that the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point condition `IsGamma1Point` is preserved by variable changes acting on `LevelPData`, that the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-kernel condition `IsGamma0PowAt` is preserved under the twisted polynomial `kernelVariableChangeDeg`, and that divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` is transported along variable changes. $\mathcal G$ is a family of relative group laws on the projective Weierstrass models over $\mathcal O$-algebras, assumed chord-and-tangent (`h𝒢`) and with identity at the origin section (`h𝒢O`); $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport` for $\mathcal G$ and $q$, assumed to be a section transport (`h𝒯`). The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every projective Weierstrass curve over an $\mathcal O$-algebra, graded ring homomorphisms realising variable changes and coefficient maps on the graded coordinate rings, with irrelevant-ideal conditions, satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom` resp. `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   **The moduli problem and its universal object.** Let $\mathcal R = \mathrm{rigidDataH1Pow}\,\mathcal O\,\ell_g\,M'\,q\,$ (`hℓ`, `hM`, `hL`, $\mathcal G$, $\mathcal T$) be the rigid Weierstrass datum whose raw points over a $T$ consist of a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with a tuple of $\Gamma_0(p^{v_p(M')})$-kernel polynomials, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ point datum and a Drinfeld $q$-basis, subject to the link condition `IsGamma1Link`. $P_0$ is a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` for the associated `LevelModuliDatum`, i.e. a ring $B_0$ with a universal point representing all points; $x_0$ is a point of that datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has Laurent expansion $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q$ (`hx₀`); `clC` is an $\mathcal O$-algebra map from $B_0$ to the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,\mathcal O\,K\,j$ (the elements of $K$ integral over $\mathcal O[j]$), and `hclC` says that `clC` followed by the inclusion into $K$ is the classifying map of $x_0$.
--
--   **The Tate-point pin `hμ`.** This hypothesis asserts the existence of a variable change $C$ over $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)$ and of a raw representative $r$ of $x_0$ over $K$ such that: the class of $r$ equals $x_0$; the scalar $C.u$, $C.r = -1/12$, $C.s = -1/2$, $C.t = 1/24$ satisfy the displayed relation between $u$ and the two coordinates of the Tate toric point $\mathrm{tateToricPoint}\,k_0\,q$ at $\zeta^q$, where $\zeta$ is the unit attached to $\xi$; the Weierstrass curve of $r$, pushed to $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)$, equals $C \bullet \mathrm{tateBase}\,k_0\,q$; for each prime $p \mid M'$, each field $F'$ with a ring map $k_0 \to F'$ and each primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta' \in F'$, the $p$-component of the level polynomial of $r$ maps to the `kernelVariableChangeDeg`-twist of the product $\prod_a (X - \mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,q\,(\zeta'^a)_1)$ over $1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p \nmid a$; the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ datum of $r$ becomes the $C$-variable change of the `LevelPData` built from the two coordinates of that Tate toric point (in the pattern $(x,y,x,y)$); and there are elements $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y$ of $K$ whose expansions are the four coordinates of the $C$-twist of $\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,q$ at $\zeta^{\ell_g}$ with vectors $(1,0)$ and $(0,-1)$, such that the Drinfeld sections $P$ and $Q$ of $r$ pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of the above, the following holds. Let $y, y'$ be maximal ideals of the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,\mathcal O\,K\,j$ and let $\psi, \psi'$ be $\mathcal O$-algebra maps from that chart algebra to $\kappa$ whose zero sets are exactly $y$ and $y'$ respectively. Assume that $\psi$ and $\psi'$ agree on all floor readings: for every $g \in \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb Q)$ lying in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}(M')$ whose image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(M')$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that $g$ is regular wherever $\mathrm{jq}$ is (i.e. $\mathrm{ord}_P \ge 0$ for $g$ at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(M')$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\mathrm{jq}$ has nonnegative order) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, and for every proof that $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g$ lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, one has $\psi$ and $\psi'$ agreeing on that element.
--
--   Then, for all raw points $x, x'$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\kappa$ such that the class of $x$ is the image of the universal point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under the map induced by $\psi \circ \mathrm{clC}$, and the class of $x'$ is the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under the map induced by $\psi' \circ \mathrm{clC}$; assuming further that the affine curve of $x$ has no nontrivial $q$-torsion over $\kappa$ (every $P$ with $q \cdot P = 0$ is $0$); and given points $g$ of the affine curve of $x$ and $g'$ of the affine curve of $x'$ such that $g$ has additive order $M'$ and, for every prime $p \mid M'$, every $n$ and every nonsingular affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n \cdot g = (x_1,y_1)$ of additive order $p^{v_p(M')}$, the $p$-component of the level polynomial of $x$ vanishes at $x_1$, and likewise for $g'$ with $x'$ — then the two classes in $\mathrm{ModuliPoint}\,M'\,\kappa$ of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-pairs $(x.\mathrm{curve}, g)$ and $(x'.\mathrm{curve}, g')$, each with the ellipticity witnessed by the unit discriminant and the order condition, coincide.
--
--   This is the fibre-identification step for the $H_1$-chart in the analysis of the $q$-adic reduction of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-structure: two closed points of the chart algebra whose readings on integral modular functions regular at the cusp agree, and whose associated curves are supersingular in the sense dictated by the place $s$, define the same point of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-moduli set over the residue field. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_place_forall_isModuliPlaceOf_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_place_forall_isModuliPlaceOf_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1) to produce a place of the reduced function field whose moduli interpretation is well defined.
